 "final_text": "Submitted. Summary for Robin:\n\n- **2 clean matches**: Alpine Ski House wire (PMT-2101, $12,400.00) and Coho Winery wire (PMT-2103, $22,000.00) tie exactly to the books.\n- **1 discrepancy**: PMT-2102 (City Power & Light ACH) \u2014 bank shows $8,105.75, books show $8,150.75. A $45.00 shortfall on the bank side, likely a fee netted off the ACH before it hit the account.\n- **1 bank-only item**: DEP-9911, $6,750.00 on 2/28, memo'd \"UNIDENTIFIED REMITTER \u2014 LOCKBOX.\" No matching AR record in books at all \u2014 needs identification before it can be applied.\n- **1 books-only item**: PMT-2104, Consolidated Messenger check #8841 for $5,325.50 (dated 2/27), posted in the AR subledger but never showed up on the bank statement \u2014 likely a check still in transit/uncleared.\n\nThe other statement lines (lockbox batches, payroll funding, FX conversions, card settlement, wire-out-supplier debits) are treasury noise unrelated to customer AR receipts and don't tie to any books entity, so I left them out of the reconciliation scope.",
